  "contract": "Native autocommit SELECT streaming uses pull-based typed candidates, borrowed KV scans and ordered overlay merging. Bounded JSON chunks and explicit row/completion records support incremental client consumption without whole-result collection. LIMIT/sink failure stop the source. Only the latest query report is retained with a cumulative count.",
  "wire_contract": "SQL_STREAM_REQUEST is exactly RSF_SQL_STREAM_V1 followed by LF. Row JSON is carried in at most 4096 decoded bytes per chunk. Ordinals, row/result byte counts, view version and terminal completion/clean EOF are validated by the public bounded decoder. Partial delivery is not success. Authorization, pending-state reconciliation and current-primary read quorum precede output.",
  "compatibility": "Legacy native SELECT retains at most 65536 JSON bytes and directs larger reads to streaming; no silent truncation. Session reads retain their existing 24576 canonical byte bound, enforced incrementally. Existing library collecting wrappers remain available. Secondary candidate filtering precedes typed projection, including committed and staged nullable rows. No durable command/checkpoint/receipt format changes.",
  "memory_scope": "Constant candidate/result-row representations, schema/query/TLS state and a 4096-byte output chunk. Result memory depends on the largest row rather than total rows. Resident data/history/receipts, cold recovery and session working-snapshot reconstruction are separate capacity concerns. Library collecting wrappers or client callbacks can choose to retain complete results.",
  "io_budget": "The existing cumulative two-second transport budget includes TLS/request/response I/O, including blocking stream writes, while excluding application CPU. Streaming does not renew the budget. This is not a query CPU deadline, resumable cursor or durable read lease.",
  "verified": [
    "borrowed ordered prefix iteration skips tombstones and remains within its prefix",
    "lazy typed execution reads no candidate beyond LIMIT or sink failure",
    "SQL staged insert/update/delete merges in primary-key order without a collected map",
    "indexed nullable candidates retain pre-projection filtering for committed and staged rows",
    "query diagnostic retention remains constant over repeated reads",
    "canonical session read-result bound is enforced before retaining each row",
    "bounded decoder rejects every truncated prefix, oversized records, malformed counts/hex, changed versions and trailing data",
    "JSON escaping and large rows survive bounded multi-chunk encoding",
    "closed output never publishes a completion; nonreading sockets exhaust the cumulative budget during application execution",
    "real TLS debug/release workloads each stream 128 rows and 264960 JSON bytes, validate every row, projection/LIMIT, empty results, buffered overflow and missing quorum",
    "both automatic takeover profiles stream from the replacement after old-primary data loss"
  ],
